module contract;

// CTraces context release — resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Card W36-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-3. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream
// function. This module verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise. Any verdict that rests on it is a
// verdict RELATIVE TO this declaration, never a proof of the C implementation.
//
// Read from the pinned checkout (`build/cycle19/fluent-bit-clang-source`) at
// Fluent Bit 66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97 on this card's own run.
//
// ## Why this callee
//
// Two projected functions in the baseline are blocked by `ctr_destroy` and by
// nothing else: `ctr_decode_msgpack_destroy`
// (`lib/ctraces/src/ctr_decode_msgpack.c:770`) and
// `ctr_decode_opentelemetry_destroy` (`:651` of its own file), each holding
// exactly one leaf. It is `cmt_destroy`'s exact sibling one library over, and
// it is declared here for the same reason and on the same reading.
//
// ## `ctr_destroy`, read from `lib/ctraces/src/ctraces.c:58-71`
//
//     void ctr_destroy(struct ctrace *ctx)
//     {
//         struct cfl_list *head;
//         struct cfl_list *tmp;
//         struct ctrace_resource_span *resource_span;
//
//         /* delete resources */
//         cfl_list_foreach_safe(head, tmp, &ctx->resource_spans) {
//             resource_span = cfl_list_entry(head, struct ctrace_resource_span, _head);
//             ctr_resource_span_destroy(resource_span);
//         }
//
//         free(ctx);
//     }
//
//   * `ctx` is the ONLY parameter, and the LAST statement on every path is
//     `free(ctx)` — unconditional. After the call the caller may not read,
//     write or release `ctx` again. That is what `resource_released` says.
//   * The nullability marker is **`nonnull`**, measured rather than defaulted:
//     there is NO leading null guard, and the first executable statement
//     dereferences the parameter, `cfl_list_foreach_safe` expanding to a read
//     of `ctx->resource_spans`. `ctr_destroy(NULL)` is undefined behaviour
//     upstream, not a tolerated no-op.
//   * The result is `void`, so `resource_return_none()` is the faithful — and
//     the only faithful — result mode.
//
// ## The cascade, stated rather than hidden
//
// The loop releases every resource span on the context's list through
// `ctr_resource_span_destroy`. No span is a tracked identity in this
// projection — each is reached only by walking `ctx`'s own intrusive list, and
// no analysed call site holds a separate binding to one. This declaration
// states the custody fact about `ctx` and says NOTHING about the cascade being
// complete or correct.
//
// ## ABI and modes (constraint 8)
//
// `lib/ctraces/include/ctraces/ctraces.h:72` declares
//
//     void ctr_destroy(struct ctrace *ctx);
//
// One object-pointer level — `ptr<mut, u8>` — and a `void` result, spelled
// `unit`. Arity one, matching every analysed call site; not variadic, so no
// `resource_variadic_data_tail()`.
//
// ## Declared although defined in a corpus unit
//
// `ctr_destroy` IS defined inside an audited unit, `ctraces/ctraces.c`, so it
// meets constraint 8's duty gate. A declared contract always wins over an
// inferred W4 summary and a disagreement is a `SummaryConflict` diagnostic,
// never a silent override; a withdrawal would be scoped to `ctraces.c` alone,
// and the two call sites this declaration exists to decide are in two OTHER
// units, which define no body for it. `ctraces.c`'s own definition stays
// analyzable and is not rewritten.
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED
//
//   * Nothing about `ctr_resource_span_destroy`, which is not declared here.
//   * Nothing about whether a context reached this call in a valid state.
//   * Nothing about double release or use-after-free, which the gateway's own
//     liveness precondition refuses on settled denotations, unchanged here.
//   * Nothing about thread safety or ordering.

// --- the CTraces context's release -----------------------------------------
extern fn ctr_destroy(ctx: ptr<mut, u8>) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_released(ctx, nonnull);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

